e welcoming a puppy home.</p>\n</div><div class=\"uagb-ifb-separator\"></div><div class=\"uagb-ifb-button-wrapper wp-block-button\"><a class=\"uagb-infobox-cta-link wp-block-button__link\" href=\"#contact-form\" onclick=\"return true;\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_self\"><span class=\"uagb-inline-editing\">Get In Touch</span><svg viewbox=\"0 0 512 512\" xmlns=\"https://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M504.3 273.6l-112.1 104c-6.992 6.484-17.18 8.218-25.94 4.406c-8.758-3.812-14.42-12.45-14.42-21.1L351.9 288H32C14.33 288 .0002 273.7 .0002 255.1S14.33 224 32 224h319.9l0-72c0-9.547 5.66-18.19 14.42-22c8.754-3.809 18.95-2.075 25.94 4.41l112.1 104C514.6 247.9 514.6 264.1 504.3 273.6z\"></path></svg></a></div></div></div>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-container uagb-block-8bb33eeb alignfull uagb-is-root-container\"><div class=\"uagb-container-inner-blocks-wrap\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-8c55b199\"><h2 class=\"uagb-heading-text\"><strong>Frequently Asked Questions About Staffies</strong></h2></div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-faq uagb-faq__outer-wrap uagb-block-fbc46549 uagb-faq-icon-row-reverse uagb-faq-layout-grid uagb-faq-expand-first-true uagb-faq-inactive-other-false uagb-faq__wrap uagb-buttons-layout-wrap uagb-faq-equal-height\" role=\"tablist\"><div class=\"wp-block-uagb-faq-child uagb-faq-child__outer-wrap uagb-faq-item uagb-block-3ebd8cbb\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"uagb-faq-questions-button uagb-faq-questions\"><h3 class=\"uagb-question\"><strong><strong>What is the difference between an Amstaff and a Staffordshire Terrier (English)?</strong> </strong></h3></div><div class=\"uagb-faq-content\"><p>The <strong>American Staffordshire Terrier (Amstaff)</strong> and the <strong>English Staffordshire Bull Terrier</strong> are two distinct breeds with different histories and standards. Amstaffs are typically larger and heavier than English Staffies. Responsible breeders do not cross these two breeds.</p></div></div><div class=\"wp-block-uagb-faq-child uagb-faq-child__outer-wrap uagb-faq-item uagb-block-206113a7\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"uagb-faq-questions-button uagb-faq-questions\"><h3 class=\"uagb-question\"><strong><strong>I’m looking into getting a Staffy puppy. Where should I start?</strong> </strong></h3></div><div class=\"uagb-faq-content\"><p>Start by finding a reputable, <strong>KC-registered</strong> breeder who performs genetic health checks. An ethical breeder will prioritize the puppy’s health and temperament and will be transparent about their breeding practices.</p></div></div><div class=\"wp-block-uagb-faq-child uagb-faq-child__outer-wrap uagb-faq-item uagb-block-34b9d733\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"uagb-faq-questions-button uagb-faq-questions\"><h3 class=\"uagb-question\"><strong><strong>How can I tell if my puppy is an American or an English Staffy?</strong></strong></h3></div><div class=\"uagb-faq-content\"><p> A definitive way to tell is by checking its pedigree papers and Kennel Club registration. An <strong>English Staffordshire Bull Terrier</strong> from the UK will be registered with <strong>The Kennel Club</strong> and will adhere to their specific breed standard, which is smaller and more compact than the American variety.</p></div></div><div class=\"wp-block-uagb-faq-child uagb-faq-child__outer-wrap uagb-faq-item uagb-block-456b6f39\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"uagb-faq-questions-button uagb-faq-questions\"><h3 class=\"uagb-question\"><strong><strong>Why weren’t Staffordshire Bull Terriers banned in the UK?</strong> </strong></h3></div><div class=\"uagb-faq-content\"><p>The <strong>Staffordshire Bull Terrier</strong> is not on the UK’s list of banned breeds. They are legally permitted in the UK due to their history as a family companion breed and their well-documented temperament as a “nanny dog.” The UK’s Dangerous Dogs Act targets breeds based on their fighting history and genetics, not their reputation.</p></div></div><div class=\"wp-block-uagb-faq-child uagb-faq-child__outer-wrap uagb-faq-item uagb-block-30e4af33\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"uagb-faq-questions-button uagb-faq-questions\"><h3 class=\"uagb-question\"><strong><strong>What are Staffies prone to?</strong></strong></h3></div><div class=\"uagb-faq-content\"><p>While generally a healthy breed, Staffies are genetically prone to two key hereditary diseases: <strong>L-2-HGA</strong> (a neurological disorder) and <strong>HC-HSF4</strong> (hereditary cataracts). This is why it is essential to buy from a breeder who can provide clear health certificates for both parent dogs. They can also be prone to skin allergies.</p></div></div><div class=\"wp-block-uagb-faq-child uagb-faq-child__outer-wrap uagb-faq-item uagb-block-84ae5bb7\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"uagb-faq-questions-button uagb-faq-questions\"><h3 class=\"uagb-question\"><strong><strong>What is the difference between a Staffy and a Pit Bull?</strong></strong></h3></div><div class=\"uagb-faq-content\"><p>The <strong>Staffordshire Bull Terrier</strong> is a distinct and officially recognized breed by The Kennel Club in the UK. The term “Pit Bull” is a general term often used to describe a type of dog, including breeds like the American Pit Bull Terrier, which are not recognized by the UK Kennel Club and are banned under the Dangerous Dogs Act. Staffies are a separate breed with a well-documented history as a family-friendly companion.</p></div></div></div></div></div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-container uagb-block-gnjoucmq alignfull uagb-is-root-container\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-info-box uagb-block-ejlgzf7y uagb-infobox__content-wrap uagb-infobox-icon-above-title uagb-infobox-image-valign-top\"><div class=\"uagb-ifb-content\"><div class=\"uagb-ifb-title-wrap\"><h2 class=\"uagb-ifb-title\"><strong>Conclusion – The BlueStaffyUK Promise</strong></h2></div><div class=\"uagb-ifb-desc\">\n<p>Choosing a puppy is a <strong>life-changing decision</strong>, and at BlueStaffyUK, we take that responsibility seriously. From <a href=\"/blue-staffy-uk-breeders/\">KC-registered breeders</a> to <a href=\"/blue-staffy-health-uk/\">health-tested parents</a>, every step of our process is designed to ensure families receive <strong>happy, healthy, ethically bred Staffordshire Bull Terrier puppies</strong>. We invite you to take the final step and join our community. To learn more about our commitment, you can read our <strong><a href=\"/privacy-policy-uk/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">privacy policy</a></strong>.</p>\n</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-info-box uagb-block-211e4392 uagb-infobox__content-wrap uagb-infobox-icon-above-title uagb-infobox-image-valign-top\"><div class=\"uagb-ifb-content\"><div class=\"uagb-ifb-title-wrap\"><h3 class=\"uagb-ifb-title\">Unlike generic classifieds, we provide:</h3></div><div class=\"uagb-ifb-desc\">\n<p>💡 <strong>Transparency</strong> – with health papers, KC registration, and parent details.<br/>🌍 <strong>Nationwide access</strong> – from <a href=\"/uk-locations/staffy-breeding-dogs-glasgow/\">Staffy breeders in Glasgow</a> to London and beyond.<br/><br/>📚 <strong>Education</strong> – through <a href=\"/blue-staffy-blog-guides/\">guides and blogs</a> tailored to first-time and experienced owners alike.<br/><br/>❤️ <strong>Community support</strong> – real testimonials, honest reviews, and trust at every step.<br/><br/>When you choose BlueStaffyUK, you’re not just buying a dog. You’re welcoming a <strong>loyal companion</strong> into your home with confidence that you’ve made the right choice.</p>\n</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-buttons uagb-buttons__outer-wrap uagb-btn__default-btn uagb-btn-tablet__default-btn uagb-btn-mobile__default-btn uagb-block-bn3vhtb4\"><div class=\"uagb-buttons__wrap uagb-buttons-layout-wrap\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-buttons-child uagb-buttons__outer-wrap uagb-block-375475b7 wp-block-button\"><div class=\"uagb-button__wrapper\"><a aria-label=\"\" class=\"uagb-buttons-repeater wp-block-button__link\" href=\"#contact-form\" rel=\"follow noopener\" role=\"button\" target=\"_self\"><div class=\"uagb-button__link\">Contact a Trusted Breeder Now</div></a></div></div>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-container uagb-block-0nilffsm alignfull uagb-is-root-container\" id=\"contact-form\"><div class=\"uagb-container-inner-blocks-wrap\"> <div class=\"wp-block-uagb-container alignfull uagb-is-root-container bsuk-contact-form-wrap\">\n<div class=\"bsuk-form-card\">\n<div class=\"bsuk-form-header\">\n<h2>🐾 Reserve Your Blue Staffy Puppy</h2>\n<p>Fill in your details below and we'll be in touch within 24 hours</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bsuk-form-body\">\n<div class=\"bsuk-form-notice\">⏰ <strong>Delivery Note:</strong> Delivery begins 24–48 hours after payment confirmation. Train station pickup is our default method (free).</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n";
